{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.HeliumBrunnianDeficitMeasured","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HeliumBrunnianDeficitMeasured","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.brunnian_deficit_sign_flip_a3_a4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.brunnian_deficit_sign_flip_a3_a4","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumBrunnianDeficitMeasured.lean#L123-L131","doc":"**(CAPSTONE) The A=3 → A=4 Milnor-parity sign FLIP (both measured).**  The A=3\nBorromean deficit is positive (`τ_Borr < 1`) while the A=4 Brunnian deficit is\nnegative (`τ_L₄ > 1`): the level trace crosses the unlink between the length-3 and\nlength-4 Milnor objects.  Contrast the merged `sign_swap_a3_a4`, which is a *residual*\nsign swap (`μ₃>0` vs `μ₄<0`) proved under the ASSUMED `τ ≤ 1`; here the *Brunnian\ndeficit itself* flips sign, measured, and that flip removes the A=4 sign wall. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.mu4_sign_compatible_measured_brunnian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.mu4_sign_compatible_measured_brunnian","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumBrunnianDeficitMeasured.lean#L107-L121","doc":"**(CAPSTONE, sign) The measured Brunnian cluster is sign-COMPATIBLE with `μ₄`.**\nBoth `μ₄ = −4.591 < 0` and the measured `c₄ = E₀·(1 − τ_L₄) < 0` are negative, so the\nsign-exclusion the merged conditional wall asserts under `τ ≤ 1` does NOT arise at the\nsubstrate: on sign grounds the genuine 4-component Brunnian binding cluster *could*\nmatch `μ₄`.  The Route-3 sign wall does **not** close unconditionally — its antecedent\nis measured false — and the A=4 recipe reopens on sign.  (This is NOT a magnitude\nderivation of `μ₄`; the magnitude test is separate and unfitted.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.brunnian4Cluster_measured_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.brunnian4Cluster_measured_neg","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumBrunnianDeficitMeasured.lean#L100-L103","doc":"The measured genuine-Brunnian cluster is negative at the substrate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.brunnian4Cluster_neg_of_tau_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.brunnian4Cluster_neg_of_tau_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumBrunnianDeficitMeasured.lean#L92-L98","doc":"**Mirror of `brunnian4Cluster_nonneg`.**  When the level trace lies *above* the\nunlink (`τ > 1`, the measured case) and the energy scale is positive, the Brunnian\ndeficit cluster is NEGATIVE. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.measured_antecedent_fails","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.measured_antecedent_fails","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumBrunnianDeficitMeasured.lean#L88-L90","doc":"**The scope-(b) antecedent `τ_L₄ ≤ 1` of the merged wall is measured FALSE.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.tauBorr3Measured_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.tauBorr3Measured_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumBrunnianDeficitMeasured.lean#L83-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.tauBorr3Measured","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.tauBorr3Measured","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumBrunnianDeficitMeasured.lean#L79-L81","doc":"Measured A=3 Borromean level trace at the substrate: `τ_Borr ≈ 0.99837 < 1`\n(the POSITIVE-deficit, O(h⁴) case that #4360 proved). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.tauL4Measured_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.tauL4Measured_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumBrunnianDeficitMeasured.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.tauL4Measured","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.tauL4Measured","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumBrunnianDeficitMeasured.lean#L71-L75","doc":"Measured genuine-Brunnian level trace at the substrate `q₀`:\n`τ_L₄ = g_link/g_unlink ≈ 1.000146 > 1` for `w₄ = [[A₀₁, A₁₂], A₂₃]` (base n=4,\nrobust to representative + convention + width-3 cabling).  This is an *empirically\nmeasured input*, cited to the witness — not a derived closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.brunnian4Cluster","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.brunnian4Cluster","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumBrunnianDeficitMeasured.lean#L64-L67","doc":"The 4-body Brunnian cluster realized as an energy-scaled trace deficit against\nthe unlink, `c₄ = E₀·(1 − τ)` (mirror of `HeliumFourBodyCluster.brunnian4Cluster`,\nwith the level trace `τ` supplied as a scalar rather than a function). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.mu4Residual_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.mu4Residual_neg","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumBrunnianDeficitMeasured.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.mu4Residual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitMeasured.mu4Residual","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumBrunnianDeficitMeasured.lean#L55-L58","doc":"The A=4 4-body simplex residual coefficient (mirror of\n`HeliumFourBodyCluster.mu4Residual`): derived, negative, the α-cluster saturation\nsignature.  The sign — not the digits — is load-bearing. ","signatureChunk":0}]}